#!/usr/bin/env bash
# =============================================================================
# setup_env — bootstrap the local Compose cluster.
# Copy each .env.example to .env, build the images, start the stack
# (migrations run automatically) and seed HQ (admin + demo menu/outlets).
# Outlet terminals start UNPROVISIONED on purpose: pair them from the UI —
# HQ console → Outlets → create → issue key → outlet /setup wizard
# (PRD §8.7, §9.2). Manual equivalent: README "Fresh clone → running system".
# =============================================================================
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")"

echo "==> Creating .env files (existing ones are kept)"
for env in .env hq-backend/.env outlet-backend/.env hq-frontend/.env outlet-frontend/.env; do
  [ -f "$env" ] || cp "${env}.example" "$env"
done

echo "==> Building images"
docker compose build

echo "==> Starting stack (hq-migrate / outlet-a-migrate run before the APIs)"
docker compose up -d

echo "==> Seeding HQ (admin + demo menu/items + demo outlets)"
docker compose run --rm -T hq-api node dist/database/seed.js

cat <<'EOF'

Setup complete. Pair the outlet terminal from the UI (the demo flow):
  1. HQ console:    http://localhost:8080  (admin@fnb.local / Admin123!)
     Outlets → create an outlet (or use a seeded demo outlet) → copy its
     Outlet ID + code from the pairing panel.
  2. Outlet A POS:  http://localhost:8081/setup
     Step 1: paste the Outlet ID + code, choose the first admin account.
  3. HQ console: the outlet's page → API keys → Issue key → copy the
     one-time key ID + secret.
  4. Outlet A POS step 2: paste the key pair → "Test & pair".
     The worker picks it up from the terminal's database (no restart).

  HQ API:       http://localhost:4000/api/v1  (Swagger: /api/v1/docs)
  Outlet A API: http://localhost:5000/api/v1  (Swagger: /api/v1/docs)

Check outlet -> HQ sync: docker compose logs -f outlet-a-worker
Reset outlet A to re-demo (wipes its database volume):
  docker rm -f fnb-platform-outlet-a-db-1 && \
  docker volume rm fnb-platform_outlet-a-db-data && docker compose up -d
EOF
